{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1191900-cod-compatability-with-previous-nwod-books","id":1191900,"title":"CoD compatability with previous nWoD books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-05T05:42:42-08:00","id":1191900,"title":"CoD compatability with previous nWoD books","content":"Can you port older (i.e. 1st edition) game material from Vampire Requiem, Werewolf Forsaken and other lines easily enough?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> SC69","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3379-space-chthuloid-1969","name":"Space Chthuloid 1969","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3379_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T05:54:19-08:00","id":1191901,"title":"","content":"Depends on the material. Setting and lore not explicitly invalidated in 2E are going to be okay. A lot of the mechanics have been reworked from the ground, so you\u2019ll need to do extensive homebrew to use them (assuming they haven\u2019t been folded into other parts of the game already).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:32:34-08:00","id":1191943,"title":"","content":"I'll assume you mean mechanical content; the majority of flavor content is compatible across editions, minus a hiccup here and there.<br /> <br /> <b>Rules impacted by the edition change, which may require overhauling or replacement outright when interacted with</b><ul><li>Sins against Morality, Harmony, or Wisdom.</li> <li>Checking the values of Morality, Harmony, or Clarity.</li> <li>Anything pertaining to derangements.</li> <li>Virtue and Vice as selections from discrete sets of 7.</li> <li>Modifying experience costs.</li> <li>Weapon bonuses.</li> <li>Rules for interacting with and the manifestation of Twilight beings like ghosts or spirits.</li> <li>For vampires, clan banes, the Predator's Taint and structure of the Coils of the Dragon.</li> <li>For werewolves, the dot structure of Gifts and the effects of Lunacy.</li> <li>For mages, spells in general, including anything involving covert or vulgar aspects in particular.</li> <li>For Prometheans, Disquiet and Wasteland progression, and the dot structure and cost of Transmutations.</li> <li>For changelings, pledges, dreamweaving, the dot structure of Contracts, and the benefits of kiths.</li> </ul>Traits not listed above are largely intact, so a Merit or a Devotion, for example, whose effects don't fall under one of the above umbrellas can likely be ported over fairly smoothly. This is off the top of my head, so I may have missed a thing or two, but it should cover the broad strokes.<br /> <br /> If you trip one of the edition changes, how much overhauling you have to do can vary. Weapon bonuses, for example, no longer grant dice to an action, but instead directly increase damage on a successful roll. You're usually okay with a 2e weapon rating of one point less than the 1e weapon bonus. Vampires use the same core Disciplines to achieve largely the same effects, but individual powers may fall on different dot levels in ways that might occasionally bother some subsidiary power that expects the wrong Animalism 1. Mage spellcasting, meanwhile, has been overhauled so thoroughly that it's a crapshoot whether a 1e spell writeup will be much more useful than rewriting from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}